<section id="coverage" class="route-band"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Supported scope</div><h2>Know what your history includes.</h2><p class="section-copy">Free includes all available supported features. Coverage depends on Shopify permissions, privacy admission, enabled observations, and retained evidence. Tracking starts after setup; it cannot recreate earlier history Shopify did not provide.</p></div><div class="coverage-table" role="region" aria-label="StoreChronicle coverage" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Supported coverage with Free access</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Store data</th><th scope="col">What to expect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Products, prices, and collections</th><td>Supported fields and membership observations, with available before-and-after values.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Inventory</th><td>Supported quantities with the required Shopify access.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Orders</th><td>A limited order summary, not the full order or customer profile. Access and privacy setup are required.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pages and themes</th><td>Configured observations of supported content. Observations do not capture every intervening edit.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Review rules and notifications</th><td>Rules flag matching changes for review. Optional notifications and summaries require service configuration and merchant opt-in.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">CSV export and read-only API</th><td>Export retained history or read it through the authenticated API. The shared API limit is 100 requests per hour per installation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="pricing-source">Restoration is selective and evidence-dependent: supported product, variant, collection, page, or inventory fields may be eligible. Order and theme restoration are not offered. StoreChronicle is not a whole-store backup.</p></div></section>
<section id="retention"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">History and restoration evidence</div><h2>Keep the record. Check the evidence.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Ordinary history has no automatic age-based expiry while installed. Activity and restoration evidence are retained for up to 120 days. Shorter merchant settings, uninstall cleanup, and privacy erasure take precedence. An ordinary history entry can remain after its restoration evidence expires; the app cannot recover previously deleted records.</p><p class="pricing-source">Read the <a href="/privacy.html#storechronicle">StoreChronicle privacy disclosure</a> for deletion, backup, and external-recipient handling.</p></div></section>
